Subject: [PATCH 03/12] launchd: TEMP DIAGNOSTIC instrumentation for bug #6
 (second-thread SIGSEGV), plus real pthread_main_thread_bootstrap() fix

Mid-investigation checkpoint, not a resolved fix -- committed for a
clean handoff to whoever continues this (see iokit repo's
docs/backlog.md item d11 and project memory
project_xnu_rpi3_launchd_pid1_2026-08-28_session2.md /
project_xnu_rpi3_static_to_dylib_sweep_2026-08-29.md for full context).

launchd.c: real iokit_diag()/iokit_diag_syscall3() raw-console
diagnostic helper + prints through main()'s early sequence (still live,
not yet reverted -- part of the same TEMP DIAGNOSTIC convention this
project already uses elsewhere, see iokit's own docs/backlog.md P3 item
3). Also a real, tested fix: main() now explicitly calls
pthread_main_thread_bootstrap() before launchd_runtime_init(),
bootstrapping launchd's own local main-thread pthread_t for the first
time (confirmed via nm this was never touched before -- the existing
dyld-constructor fix only ever bootstrapped libsystem_pthread.dylib's
separate copy). Real and correct, but confirmed NOT to fix bug #6 on
its own -- the SIGSEGV in the second thread persists.

runtime.c: iokit_diag8() helper + prints through
launchd_runtime_init()/runtime_add_mport()/kqueue_demand_loop() -- the
second thread's own entry point, where bug #6's real crash happens
(mig_get_reply_port, right after select() returns).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DF4f2tcNW24JcVKMUujSFt
