From 2f0ef341abb46a2f541a39797bd9a52bc55c75ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anurodh Pokharel <anurodhp@icloud.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 14:05:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06/12] launchd: drop redundant pthread main-thread bootstrap +
 strip diagnostics

launchd's main() explicitly called pthread_main_thread_bootstrap(). That
was actively harmful, not merely redundant.

__main_thread is an EXTERNAL COMMON symbol defined in both launchd.macho
and libsystem_pthread.dylib, so the two coalesce at runtime into a single
struct. __pthread_ptr_munge_token is NON-external in both and does NOT
coalesce. By the time main() runs, libSystem.B.dylib's constructor has
already bootstrapped that shared struct via libsystem_pthread.dylib's
copy, signing it with that image's private token. Calling launchd's own
copy here re-signed it with a SECOND token, after which every
pthread_self() served by libsystem_pthread.dylib -- the copy real
CoreFoundation, libdispatch and libc++ actually bind to -- failed
_pthread_validate_signature() and called abort_with_reason(): a silent
exit(1), signal 0, with zero console output.

The authoritative bootstrap already runs before any initializer or
main(), so the correct number of additional bootstraps here is zero.
launchd.macho no longer links a static pthread copy at all (see
tools/userland_staging/build_launchd.sh in the parent repo).

Also strips the pd_diag_console() helper and all TEMP DIAGNOSTIC markers
from the prior bisection. Those markers wrote to /dev/console, which
cannot distinguish "never called" from "called, write failed" -- they
produced a confident false negative that sent the investigation after
dyld's pre-main() bootstrap instead of this bug.

Real launchd now boots as PID 1 and reaches launchd_runtime().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Nkfdgj4zUvAa7XcRLcWBgt
