From a575c424e17ad14d3243bcc501ebdebd95611a3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anurodh Pokharel <anurodhp@icloud.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 16:04:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] launchd: remount / read-write before
 pid1_prepare_legacy_ipc()

pd_launchd_boot() -- whose first act is the real `mount -uw /`
equivalent this port needs, because vfs_mountroot() hardcodes
MNT_RDONLY|MNT_ROOTFS -- ran after jobmgr_init(), which is too late.
pd_pid1_prepare_legacy_ipc() runs before it and writes to that same
still-read-only root, producing the

    mkdir("/var/tmp/"): Read-only file system

error in every launchd PID-1 boot log up to launchd_boot_test95.log.
The remount always succeeded, just after the directories it was needed
for.

On real Darwin the root filesystem is already read-write by the time
launchd's own /var/tmp setup runs, so remounting before it -- rather
than reordering Apple's own setup code -- is the faithful fix. Nothing
between the new call site and the old one writes to disk or needs /dev
mounted (console logging goes through launchd_console, opened earlier),
so moving it up is safe as well as correct.

Verified by real QEMU boot (iokit project,
qemu/launchd_boot_test109_clean.log): the mkdir error is gone.

NOTE this reorder also made a long-latent bug reachable for the first
time: ipc_server_init() used to bail out at mkdir(LAUNCHD_SOCK_PREFIX)
returning EROFS, several statements before its atexit(ipc_clean_up)
call -- and atexit() hung forever in this port on an uninitialized
__atexit. Fixed separately on the iokit side; see
docs/launchd-pid1-postmortem.md there.
