real exec of /usr/bin/login (system_cmds/login.tproj, iokit project's
tools/userland_staging/build_login.sh) -- the real username+password
prompt this boot path has never had. login(1) itself now determines the
authenticated account's LOGNAME/USER/HOME/SHELL/PATH via real
crypt(3)/master.passwd auth and execs that account's real shell; this
helper only still sets PATH/TERM as login(1)'s own pre-auth environment
(both get overwritten/preserved by login.c itself per its real,
unmodified semantics -- see build_login.sh's own header for the full
writeup).

